<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>netstandard2.1</TargetFramework>
        <ImplicitUsings>false</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <PropertyGroup>
        <PackageId>SetNet.Ticks</PackageId>
        <Version>1.0.0</Version>
        <AssemblyVersion>1.0.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
        <FileVersion>1.0.0.0</FileVersion>
        <Authors>Artem Lemeshev</Authors>
        <Description>The tick foundation for SetNet: the ITickable / IAsyncTickable contracts, the ITickHost registration seam + ambient TickHost.Current, and the TickScheduler central update loop. Register anything into a named channel with its own rate (Hz) and priority; the scheduler drives them all from one place — 30 Hz movement, 10 Hz AI, 1 Hz housekeeping — with per-channel fixed timestep. Drive it with an internal timer (Start) or pump it from your own loop (Pump), Unity-friendly. Set one MakeCurrent() host and SetNet's game-loop modules (Mobs, Locomotion, Spawning) auto-subscribe. Zero dependencies — the game-loop modules depend on THIS, not the other way round, so SetNet core stays a pure transport.</Description>
        <PackageTags>networking;game-loop;tick;scheduler;update;ai;game;setnet</PackageTags>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Povstalez/SetNet.git</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Povstalez/SetNet</PackageProjectUrl>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
      <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
      <None Include="../../../assets/icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Visible="false" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <!-- Zero SetNet dependencies on purpose: this is a foundation the game-loop modules depend on. -->

</Project>
